
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">John Voorhees has <a href="https://www.macstories.net/reviews/a-closer-look-at-apples-upcoming-creator-studio-update/">been testing the upcoming Creator Studio updates</a>, including beta MCP support for Pages, Numbers, and Keynote. His report gives us an early look at AI agents working directly with those apps.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There are some practical details worth knowing. The app has to be open, and if you have several windows open, the agent needs to identify the one it should work on.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Keynote is getting a new interchange format, too, designed to make presentations easier for other tools to work with.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I keep beating the drum that productivity apps need to adapt for use with agentic AI going forward, and I&#8217;m glad to see the iWork team is getting on board.</p>
